# Brand and prose

## Names

- Product: Good Standing
- Trading: Good Standing Software (no Ltd)
- Legal: Good Standing Software Ltd (17423889)
- Never write that the company “trades as Good Standing”

## Document titles

Home: `Good Standing | …` (brand first). Other pages: `{Topic} | Good Standing` (brand last). Separator is `|` only — not an em dash or hyphen. Use the product name Good Standing, not the trading or legal name. Keep `<title>`, `og:title`, and `twitter:title` the same string on each page. If JSON-LD `WebPage` `name` (or `headline`) duplicates the document title, keep that in sync too.

Locked titles:

- Home: `Good Standing | software for UK membership bodies`
- Privacy: `Privacy notice | Good Standing`
- Thanks: `Thanks | Good Standing`

## Voice

- Holding pages and `/thanks/` use company **we**, not “I’m Mark…”
- Approachable, professional, intriguing. Not matey. Not salesy.
- Research before product; nothing to buy. No product-launch CTA grid.
- Do not use “CPD” in marketing, survey, or outreach blurbs — say continuing education, fees, membership, or good standing as the sentence needs
- Outreach is first-person Mark (Director) and lives in Gmail — do not invent email files here. See Outreach below.

## Tone by surface

- Home / thanks: letterhead marketing — short, research posture
- Privacy: ICO-style notice — clarity and consistency, not intrigue. Do not gut the legal structure or rewrite it for spacing or tone
- Outreach email: first-person Mark; same letter to everyone; research posture, not a pitch

## Outreach

Every recipient gets the same subject and body. Do not assume we know anything about the target organisation — no org name in the subject, no AMS, hours, register, size, or other on-file facts in the copy.

The only things that change per send:

- `To`
- Survey URL query params `ref` and `email` (`email` URL-encoded)

Do not add `organisation=`, per-org `utm_content`, or any other query param. Site and privacy links stay identical on every send.

Locked subject: `A short survey`

Locked body:

```
Hi, I'm Mark from Good Standing Software. We're researching how UK professional bodies handle membership, fees and good standing.

Before building anything, we want to know whether there's a real need — and where the manual work gets messy enough that software would actually help.

The survey is confidential, there's nothing to buy, and it takes about 5–7 minutes:
https://research.goodstanding.co.uk/r/Bz5oLN?ref={ref}&email={urlencoded-email}

Thanks in advance,

Mark
https://goodstanding.co.uk/?utm_source=survey&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=research

To opt out, reply stop.

Privacy policy: https://goodstanding.co.uk/privacy/?utm_source=survey&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=research

Good Standing Software Ltd, company no. 17423889
71–75 Shelton Street, London WC2H 9JQ
```

- Close is `Thanks in advance,` then `Mark` — not `Thanks,`
- Footer always includes company number, Shelton Street address, and `To opt out, reply stop.`
- Gmail may wrap links in `google.com/url?q=` when a draft is read back — that is Gmail, not extra copy. Write the clean URLs above.
- Drafts live in Gmail (`mark@goodstanding.co.uk`). Do not invent email files in this repo.
- Do not mark CRM Survey status Link sent or set Last surveyed until Mark actually sends.

## Links

- Internal directory links keep a trailing slash (`privacy/`, `../`, `./`)

## Consistency checklist

When editing public HTML, check these in one pass:

- Titles / `og:title` / `twitter:title` (and matching JSON-LD name) in sync
- Brand position: home brand-first; inner pages topic-first
- Separator is `|` in titles only; body copy may keep em dashes
- We-voice on holding pages
- Names lock (product / trading / legal)
- Meta descriptions match the page’s actual purpose (privacy is a notice, not a product pitch)
- H1 aligns with the title topic (`Thanks` on `/thanks/`)
- Internal directory links keep a trailing slash; footer Survey uses `?ref=footer`; homepage survey uses `?ref=homepage`
- External links follow the site pattern (`target="_blank"` `rel="noopener noreferrer"`)

## Out of this repo

- Do not edit Tally form content or drive Tally via API from here
- Do not invent outreach email files
